## 2. Core Elemental Reaction Frameworks

### A. Amplifying Reactions (Melt / Vaporise)
These do not create a standalone second number; they function entirely as straight scaling multipliers on top of the initial triggering hit:
$$Amp\ Reaction = Reaction\ Base\ Multiplier \times \left(1 + \frac{2.78 \times EM}{1400 + EM} + Reaction\ DMG\ Bonus\%\right)$$
* **Forward (2.0×):** Pyro triggered on Hydro aura (Vape) / Pyro triggered on Cryo aura (Melt).
* **Reverse (1.5×):** Hydro triggered on Pyro aura (Vape) / Cryo triggered on Pyro aura (Melt).

### B. Transformative Reactions (Swirl, Overload, Superconduct, Electro-Charged, Hyperbloom)
These compute entirely separate flat damage values. They completely ignore the character's ATK, Talent%, and enemy DEF calculations, scaling strictly with Level and EM:
$$Transformative\ DMG = Reaction\ Multiplier \times Level\ Multiplier \times \left(1 + \frac{16 \times EM}{2000 + EM} + Reaction\ DMG\ Buff\%\right) \times Enemy\ RES\ Mult$$
* **Standard Level 90 Multiplier Constant ($Level\ Mult$):** Baseline value is exactly **1446.85**.
* **Reaction Multipliers:** 
  * Superconduct: 0.50 | Swirl: 0.60 | Electro-Charged: 1.20 | Overload: 2.75 | Hyperbloom / Burgeon: 3.00.

### C. Additive Reactions (Spread / Aggravate)
These act as a flat addition to your base scaling value before damage multipliers calculate, matching the structure of the BoL/Masque mechanics:
$$Additive\ Base\ DMG\ Bonus = Reaction\ Multiplier \times Level\ Multiplier \times \left(1 + \frac{5 \times EM}{1200 + EM} + Reaction\ DMG\ Buff\%\right)$$
* **Reaction Multipliers:** Aggravate: 1.15 | Spread: 1.25.

